# Dockerfile Pattern

Multi-stage build for fast pull and cold start on Azure Container Apps:

```dockerfile
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:10.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY ["juskel.Api/juskel.Api.csproj", "juskel.Api/"]
RUN dotnet restore "juskel.Api/juskel.Api.csproj"
COPY . .
WORKDIR "/src/juskel.Api"
RUN dotnet publish "juskel.Api.csproj" -c Release -o /app/publish /p:UseAppHost=false

FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0 AS final
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/publish .
ENV ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://+:8080
EXPOSE 8080
USER app
ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "juskel.Api.dll"]
```

Adjust project path/name to match the actual `.csproj`. Use `/p:UseAppHost=false` to keep the image lean.
